From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] ssl.SocketFactory.provider =
 KktlsDefaultSSLSocketFactory, standalone Conscrypt when installed

Port of libcore/0025 of the 4.4 series, the same KktlsDefaultSSLSocketFactory source byte for byte. The default
SSLSocketFactory becomes io.github.hsw.kktls.KktlsDefaultSSLSocketFactory, a new class in luni, so it is in core.jar
on the boot class path, where SSLSocketFactory.getDefault() needs it. It uses standalone Conscrypt (BoringSSL, TLS 1.3)
when /system/framework/kktls-conscrypt.jar exists, loaded together with kktls-sslfilter.jar and
libkktls_conscrypt_jni.so by its own PathClassLoader (never boot jars, so an app's own Conscrypt is not shadowed),
unless the system property persist.kktls.conscrypt is 0. Otherwise, and if Conscrypt fails to load (logged once per
process), it is the platform org.apache.harmony.xnet.provider.jsse.OpenSSLSocketFactoryImpl, the previous value:
without the Conscrypt files nothing changes. Before its loader opens the library, the factory checks its ELF header
(every PT_LOAD segment ends within the file) and, for ARM, that the CPU has NEON (AT_HWCAP of /proc/self/auxv, else
the Features line of /proc/cpuinfo): a truncated library would be SIGBUS, a NEON-less CPU SIGILL, in the linker.
Either failure is a load failure as above. libkktls_compat.so (4.1 and 4.2: the bionic functions the library needs)
gets the same ELF check when it exists. A load failure, or a failure to make the Conscrypt factory, is kept for the
process: no retry.

Two differences from 4.4, both decided by what the platform has: the platform factory is the harmony class (the 4.4
com.android.org.conscrypt one does not exist here), and Conscrypt's SSLContext returns for SDK_INT < 22 its KitKat
adapter factory, whose sockets extend 4.4's com.android.org.conscrypt.OpenSSLSocketImpl, so every createSocket would
throw NoClassDefFoundError here; the factory takes the adapter's inner org.conscrypt.OpenSSLSocketFactoryImpl instead.
Only this property changes: the security.provider order and ssl.ServerSocketFactory.provider stay as they are.
